from c8e_base import *
LB(8,5,'Language work: vocabulary, collective nouns, eye idioms, the suffix -ish, sounds and a talk','Language work for the poem on the magnifying glass: vocabulary, collective nouns, idioms with eye and the suffix -ish','Words that a magnifying glass reveals',
 "A magnifying glass shows the tiny wonders of nature that our eyes miss: a spider, a hive of bees and even the moon within reach. The language work of this poem builds our vocabulary, collective nouns, idioms with the word eye and the suffix -ish, and helps us speak about space and inventions.",
 [("Six useful words are woven, myriad, deft, stumble, surpass and marvellous. Woven means made by crossing threads, and here it means skilfully joined together. Myriad means countless, deft means quick and skilful, stumble upon means to find by chance, surpass means to go beyond, and marvellous means wonderful.","woven, myriad, deft, stumble, surpass, marvellous"),
  ("In the book's passage, a marvellous description, a story woven with fascinating details, a deft storytelling technique, myriad emotions, stumble upon twists and turns, and twists that surpass our understanding complete the paragraph.","filling the blanks in order"),
  ("A collective noun names a group. The poem uses 'a hive of bees'. In the same way we say a swarm of locusts, a constellation of stars, a grove of trees, a troupe of dancers, a battalion of soldiers and a fleet of ships.","a swarm of locusts, a fleet of ships"),
  ("An idiom has a meaning different from its separate words. The apple of one's eye is a person who is very precious. In the blink of an eye means something that happens very quickly.","apple of one's eye; in the blink of an eye"),
  ("To keep an eye on someone means to watch closely. To turn a blind eye is to act as if you do not see or notice. To see eye to eye is to agree with each other, and a bird's-eye view is an overall look at something, as if from above.","keep an eye on, turn a blind eye, see eye to eye, bird's-eye view"),
  ("The poet uses the adjective 'tigerish' by adding the suffix -ish to the noun tiger. In the same way girl gives girlish, boy gives boyish and book gives bookish. The suffix -ish means like or somewhat like the noun.","suffix -ish"),
  ("Not every noun takes -ish; for glass we make glassy and for silk we make silken or silky. When unsure, check a dictionary.","check a dictionary"),
  ("For the listening task you hear a father and daughter talk about lesser-known Indian inventions. Read all six statements first, then mark the four that are true, listening for the attitude of the speakers, such as pride, excitement and surprise.","listening task"),
  ("For the speaking task, learn the difference between the sounds f and v. For both, the lower lip lightly touches the upper teeth. The v sound has a vibration, but the f sound does not.","f and v sounds"),
  ("Practise f in forest, flowers, from, deft, afternoon, of and itself, and v in vase, valour, victory, woven, even, marvellous and hive.","f and v words"),
  ("Another speaking task asks which planet you would visit and why, with five things you would take. A third asks about a wonder invention you would make: say what it is, how it works and why it is needed, giving reasons.","speak with reasons")],
 ("Match 'a fleet of' with the right word and say what 'turn a blind eye' means.",
  [("A fleet of ships.","A fleet is a group of ships."),
   ("To turn a blind eye is to act as if you do not see or notice something.","It is an idiom, so it cannot be explained word by word.")]),
 ("Explain what a collective noun is and give two examples.",
  ["a collective noun names a group of people, animals or things","a correct example such as a swarm of locusts","a second correct example such as a grove of trees"],
  ["Thinking a collective noun names only one person","Using the wrong group word, such as a fleet of locusts"]),
 ["Woven, myriad, deft, stumble, surpass and marvellous are useful words from the lesson.","Collective nouns: swarm of locusts, constellation of stars, grove of trees, troupe of dancers, battalion of soldiers, fleet of ships.","Eye idioms: apple of one's eye, in the blink of an eye, keep an eye on, turn a blind eye, see eye to eye, bird's-eye view.","The suffix -ish makes adjectives: girlish, boyish, bookish.","The v sound vibrates, the f sound does not."],
 [mcq("v5b-1",1,"'a constellation of' goes with","stars",[("ships","A group of ships is a fleet."),("trees","A group of trees is a grove.")],"A constellation of stars."),
  mcq("v5b-2",1,"A group of dancers is called","a troupe",[("a battalion","A battalion is a group of soldiers."),("a swarm","A swarm is a group of locusts or bees.")],"A troupe of dancers."),
  mcq("v5b-3",1,"'The apple of one's eye' means","a person who is very precious",[("a fruit","It is an idiom, not a fruit."),("a quick event","That is in the blink of an eye.")],"An idiom has its own meaning."),
  mcq("v5b-4",1,"'In the blink of an eye' means","very quickly",[("very slowly","It is the opposite."),("very carefully","It is not about care.")],"It means something happens very quickly."),
  mcq("v5b-5",1,"To 'turn a blind eye' is to","act as if you do not notice",[("watch closely","That is keep an eye on."),("agree with someone","That is see eye to eye.")],"It means pretending not to see."),
  mcq("v5b-6",2,"Which word means 'countless'?","myriad",[("deft","Deft means quick and skilful."),("woven","Woven means joined together.")],"Myriad means countless."),
  mcq("v5b-7",2,"To 'stumble upon' something is to","find it by chance",[("fall down on it","It does not mean falling."),("lose it","It means finding it.")],"Stumble upon means finding by chance."),
  mcq("v5b-8",2,"Adding -ish to 'boy' makes the adjective","boyish",[("boyly","This is not a word."),("boying","This is not an adjective.")],"Boy plus -ish is boyish."),
  mcq("v5b-9",2,"Which idiom means 'to agree with each other'?","see eye to eye",[("keep an eye on","This means to watch closely."),("bird's-eye view","This means an overall look.")],"See eye to eye."),
  mcq("v5b-10",2,"Which word begins with the /v/ sound?","valour",[("forest","Forest begins with /f/."),("flowers","Flowers begins with /f/.")],"Valour begins with /v/."),
  mcq("v5b-11",3,"A 'bird's-eye view' is","an overall look from above",[("a close look at a bird","It is an idiom."),("a bird's dream","It is not about dreams.")],"A bird's-eye view is an overall look."),
  mcq("v5b-12",3,"Which pair is correct?","a fleet of ships; a grove of trees",[("a fleet of trees; a grove of ships","The group words are swapped."),("a swarm of ships; a fleet of stars","These pairings are wrong.")],"A fleet of ships and a grove of trees.")])
